  "summary": "Malicious code in boxy-fixture-allure (npm)",
  "details": "On require(), the package downloads a binary payload from one of four Cloudflare Workers C2 hosts (oob-worker[.]cf99-9b3[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev) via HTTPS GET to /pkg/package (or platform-specific paths /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, /pkg/package.exe). If HTTPS fails, it falls back to DNS TXT-record-based payload retrieval from subdomains of well1[.]site (tin[.]dl[.]well1[.]site, tina[.]dl[.]well1[.]site, ldr[.]dl[.]well1[.]site, win[.]dl[.]well1[.]site). The downloaded binary is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u003crandom-hex\u003e (Linux/macOS) or C:\\Windows\\Temp\\dotnet_diag_\u003crandom-hex\u003e.exe (Windows) and executed as a detached background process.",
